%% HAND-CURATED. Production-mode workflow per sys-15 §3-5; AT command protocol 921600 8N1.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Operator
    participant FactoryCLI
    participant Device
    participant IntermediateCA
    participant Gateway
    participant DeviceService
    participant LabelPrinter
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over Operator,PostgreSQL: Phase 1 — Flash + Boot Verify
    Operator->>FactoryCLI: tbot-provision start --port COM3 --batch B2026-042
    FactoryCLI->>Device: flash factory firmware via UART
    FactoryCLI->>Device: AT+STATUS
    alt flash_or_boot_failed
        Device--xFactoryCLI: timeout or ERROR
        FactoryCLI-->>Operator: FAIL Phase 1 — quarantine for repair
    else success
        Device-->>FactoryCLI: READY
    end

    Note over Operator,PostgreSQL: Phase 2 — Certificate Provisioning
    FactoryCLI->>Device: AT+CSR_GENERATE
    Device->>Device: generate EC P-256 keypair via hardware TRNG — store priv key in eFuse (never extractable)
    Device-->>FactoryCLI: PEM CSR + OK
    FactoryCLI->>FactoryCLI: parse + validate CSR
    alt csr_invalid_format
        FactoryCLI-->>Operator: FAIL Phase 2 — quarantine
    else csr_curve_mismatch (not secp256r1)
        FactoryCLI-->>Operator: FAIL Phase 2 — wrong curve
    else cn_invalid
        FactoryCLI-->>Operator: FAIL Phase 2 — CN must start with TBT-
    else success
        FactoryCLI->>IntermediateCA: sign CSR (validate: EC P-256, CN=TBT-*, 10yr validity, key usage=digital_signature+client_auth)
        IntermediateCA-->>FactoryCLI: signed X.509 cert PEM
        FactoryCLI->>Device: AT+CERT_INSTALL={signed cert PEM}
        alt cert_install_failed
            Device--xFactoryCLI: ERROR
            FactoryCLI-->>Operator: FAIL Phase 2
        else success
            Device-->>FactoryCLI: OK
        end
    end

    Note over Operator,PostgreSQL: Phase 3 — Hardware Validation (27 tests)
    FactoryCLI->>Device: AT+SERIAL
    Device-->>FactoryCLI: TBT-2026-{6digits}
    loop each test in suite (mic SNR, speaker SPL, servo, display, wifi, ble, battery, NVS, flash, heap, thermal)
        FactoryCLI->>Device: AT+TEST_{name}
        Device-->>FactoryCLI: {measured_value}
        FactoryCLI->>FactoryCLI: compare vs pass criteria + criticality flag
    end

    alt critical_test_failed
        FactoryCLI->>PostgreSQL: INSERT factory_test_results {overall_result='fail', …} then INSERT factory_test_items[]
        FactoryCLI-->>Operator: FAIL — quarantine for repair {failed_tests}
    else success
        Note over Operator,PostgreSQL: Phase 4 — Production Finalize
        FactoryCLI->>Device: AT+FLASH_PRODUCTION
        Device-->>FactoryCLI: OK (reboots into production FW)

        FactoryCLI->>Gateway: POST /v1/devices/register (mTLS, factory cred) {serial_number, hardware_revision, firmware_version}
        Gateway->>DeviceService: forward
        DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT devices {status='factory_new', lifecycle_state='unassigned'}
        DeviceService-->>FactoryCLI: 201 {device_id}

        FactoryCLI->>Gateway: POST /v1/factory/devices/:deviceId/certificate {certificate_pem}
        Gateway->>DeviceService: forward
        DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT device_certificates ON CONFLICT (fingerprint) DO NOTHING
        DeviceService-->>FactoryCLI: 201

        alt backend_register_failed
            DeviceService--xFactoryCLI: 5xx
            FactoryCLI-->>Operator: FAIL — re-run register only (idempotent on cert fingerprint)
        else success
            FactoryCLI->>PostgreSQL: INSERT factory_test_results {overall_result='pass', device_id, factory_batch_id, serial_number, test_duration_ms, operator_id, workstation_id} then INSERT factory_test_items[] (27 rows)
            FactoryCLI->>LabelPrinter: print QR label (serial + device_id)
            alt label_printer_failed
                LabelPrinter--xFactoryCLI: error
                FactoryCLI-->>Operator: WARN — manual re-print, device still PASS
            else success
                LabelPrinter-->>FactoryCLI: ok
            end
            FactoryCLI-->>Operator: PASS — ready for boxing
        end
    end

    Note over Operator,PostgreSQL: timeout 60s per AT bucket · 921600 8N1 UART · private key NEVER leaves eFuse · pilot mode <150 units / production mode >500 units with test jig
